DESCRIPTION

You turn the target’s skull into a conflagration from the inside out. The target takes 6d6 fire damage and is blinded. They then catch on fire taking 3d6 fire each round. The target remains blinded for as long as they are on fire. A successful initial Fortitude save halves the fire damage and negates the blinding and catching on fire. Then each round they can attempt to put out the fire with a Reflex save against this spell’s DC. The ongoing fire damage does not stack with other fire damage dealt from being on fire.

); Spell Resistance yes

DESCRIPTION

You radiate a magical aura that damages any undead or evil outsiders that come within 30 feet of you. Undead and evil outsiders take 2d6 points of holy damage (Will save for half) every round they stay within your radius of effect, and evil outsiders must succeed on a Will save to remain within the radius after taking damage. This spell stacks with any other “aura”-type abilities you may be using, and denies undead within its radius the advantages of desecration.

This spell functions like @UUID[Compendium.pf1.spells.53dyu81yaw4y0nz4]{Glyph of Warding}, except that a greater blast glyph deals up to 10d8 points of damage, and a greater spell glyph can store a spell of 6th level or lower.

@UUID[Compendium.pf1.spells.j0bc0iii8zp1jiwr]{Read Magic} allows you to identify a greater Glyph of Warding with a DC 16 @UUID[Compendium.pf1.pf1e-rules.x175kVqUfLGPt8tC.JournalEntryPage.VRD7jxiIAxKPt6EF]{Spellcraft} check.

Material Component: You trace the glyph with incense, which must first be sprinkled with powdered diamond worth at least 400 gp.
